# Code owners for documentation.
#
# This file only auto-requests review on PRs touching the paths below. It does
# not block merges: the "main — pull request review" ruleset now sets
# `required_approving_review_count: 0` and `require_code_owner_review: false`.
#
# Why: with a single maintainer, who authors every PR, and GitHub disallowing
# self-approval, a 1-review requirement could never be satisfied — so every
# merge went through the Admin bypass. A rule that is bypassed every time
# protects nothing and makes the bypass routine, which is how a real block
# eventually gets waved through too. Merges are gated on the required status
# checks instead ("main — required checks", which has no bypass actors).
#
# If a second maintainer joins, raise the review count back to 1 and re-enable
# `require_code_owner_review` — at that point both become satisfiable.

